          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.562,
            0.047,
            0.847,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Expressions Using Letter-Numbers"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.088,
            0.848,
            0.145
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The expression means 5 times c is added to 3 times c is added to 10 times c. So in total, the letter-number c is added "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( 5 + 3 + 1 0 )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " times. This is what we have seen as the distributive property of numbers. Thus,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.319,
            0.149,
            0.68,
            0.167
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_8_equation_3.jpg",
          "content": "5 \\times c + 3 \\times c + 10 \\times c = (5 + 3 + 10) \\times c"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.265,
            0.179,
            0.732,
            0.198
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(5 + 3 + 10) × c can be simplified to "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 8 \\times c = 1 8 c ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.212,
            0.766,
            0.236
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ If "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "c = \\mp 5 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , find the total amount earned by the scale of pencils."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.254,
            0.846,
            0.294
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Write the expression for the total money earned by selling erasers. Then, simplify the expression."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.304,
            0.848,
            0.343
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The expression for the total money earned by selling pencils and erasers during these three days is 18c + 11d."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.35,
            0.663,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Can the expression 18c + 11d be simplified further?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.381,
            0.848,
            0.419
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "There is no way of further simplifying this expression as it contains different letter-numbers. It is in its simplest form."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.419,
            0.848,
            0.458
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In this problem, we saw the expression 5c + 3c + 10c getting simplified to the expression 18c."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.465,
            0.848,
            0.506
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Check that both expressions take the same value when c is replaced by different numbers."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.525,
            0.848,
            0.566
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 6:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " A big rectangle is split into two smaller rectangles as shown. Write an expression describing the area of the bigger rectangle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.211,
            0.57,
            0.787,
            0.715
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 13,
              "bbox": [
                0.211,
                0.57,
                0.787,
                0.715
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_8_image_13.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.734,
            0.847,
            0.808
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The areas of the smaller rectangles are 4v sq. units and 3v sq. units. The area of the bigger rectangle can be found in two ways: (i) by directly using its side lengths v and (4 + 3), or (ii) by adding the areas of the smaller rectangles."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.808,
            0.848,
            0.864
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The first way gives 7v, and the second way gives "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 \\nu   +   3 \\nu"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . We know that they are equal: "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4v + 3v = 7v,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and this is the required expression for the area of the bigger rectangle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.864,
            0.848,
            0.902
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "As earlier, a big rectangle is split into two smaller rectangles as shown below. Write an expression to find the area of the rectangle AEFD."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 17,
